  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh Advancing Development &amp; Growth through Energy (BADGE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s Bangladesh Advancing Development and Growth through Energy (BADGE) activity promotes energy security and resilience through improved access to affordable, dependable, and sustainable energy systems. With FY 2024 funds, the activity will provide technical assistance, advisory services, and capacity building training to public and private sector players, and develop tools, strategy documents, and recommendation papers for government agencies. The activity will also collaborate with local, regional, and international organizations to build platforms for technology and knowledge transfer in advanced energy domains by facilitating partnerships with the commercial sector, academic institutions, and scientific laboratories. It will conduct multiple policy assessments and make policy recommendations for building an enabling environment suitable for scaling up renewable energy use in Bangladesh. This will include a review of the national energy policy, private power generating policy, guidelines, and other pertinent global renewable energy policies and practices. The activity will also take a Gender Equity and Social Inclusion (GESI) approach to planning, implementing, and making decisions about its interventions. The energy sector remains a male-dominated industry globally. By boosting women&apos;s participation in the workforce and including GESI into all BADGE interventions, the GoB and the U.S. benefit from the enhanced diversity, efficiency, and profitability of the energy sector.BADGE contributes to the U.S. Government&apos;s Indo-Pacific Strategy, particularly the Asia Enhancing Developing and Growth through Energy (Asia EDGE) initiative. Funding contributes to the Private Sector Engagement ($200,000), Innovation ($1m), and Gender Equality and Women Empowerment Secondary ($600k),earmarks and key issues.</narrative>
  </description>
